<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Donn de Burgh, 3rd Earl of Ulster</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1312–1333</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as William de Burgh, 3rd Earl of Ulster, Brown Earl</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Donn de Burgh, 3rd Earl of Ulster, the 'Brown Earl', was the Anglo-Norman lord of Ulster and much of Connacht. His murder by his own followers at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carrickfergus">Carrickfergus</a> in 1333 left only an infant daughter, and his kinsmen seized the de Burgh lands in Connacht, founding the Gaelicised lordships of Clanricarde and Mac William Iochtar.</p></div>
